  "id": "COMPOUND:8005 - PROTEIN:802",
  "verbalization": "Cobicistat is implicated in targeting the Proteasome subunit beta type-5 through two distinct pathways. The first pathway links cobicistat to the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B, which is a target of PF-03187207, and ultimately to the Proteasome subunit beta type-5. The second pathway connects cobicistat to the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 5A, which is a target of Arecoline, also leading to the same subunit. These two pathways suggest that cobicistat may exert its effects through different molecular mechanisms, both targeting the same downstream component. The integration of these evidence points implies that cobicistat could influence the proteasome through either the 5-HT2B or 5-HT5A receptors, highlighting a potential role in modulating proteasome activity. The evidence supports a mechanism where cobicistat may act as a modulator of proteasome function, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
